  "body": "If you love golf and the coast, this is a location that is hard to beat. Bordering Whangaparaoa Golf Course, the home enjoys an outlook across the fairways and towards the northern coastline, with views from the deck, dining area and even more impressive outlooks from upstairs.\r\n\r\nInside, the home is beautifully presented, with a modernised kitchen forming the centre of the living space. The open-plan dining and lounge connect easily with the deck, making the most of the outlook and giving you a front-row seat to the golf course beyond.\r\n\r\nThere are three bedrooms, including one downstairs and two upstairs, along with an additional upstairs study providing useful space for working from home, hobbies or guests. Two bathrooms, one on each level, add practicality for families and visitors.\r\n\r\nA double internal-access garage, attic storage, full insulation and a heat pump complete the practical side of the home, while the low-maintenance layout makes it easy to simply enjoy the setting.\r\n\r\nFrom here, you are within walking distance of the local primary school and bus stop, with Wentworth College, Shakespear Regional Park, Gulf Harbour Marina, beaches, cafés, restaurants and coastal walks all close by.\r\n\r\nFor golfers, having the course literally on your doorstep is hard to replicate. Add the coastal views and Gulf Harbour lifestyle, and this is a property that offers something genuinely special.",
